<title>INDIA: India Bombay Dyeing 96/97 net down.</title>
<headline>India Bombay Dyeing 96/97 net down.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  223.5  vs   1,027.5</p>
<p>    Net sales	 4,570.9  vs   7,274.2</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)    11.48 vs	55.65</p>
<p>    Other income	838.6  vs     461.7</p>
<p>    Total revenue   5,409.5  vs   7,735.9</p>
<p>    Expenditure     4,362.6  vs   5,901.2</p>
<p>    Interest	    577.1  vs     415.1</p>
<p>    Depreciation	228.3  vs     208.0</p>
<p>    Gross profit	469.8  vs   1,419.6</p>
<p>    Taxation	     18.0  vs     184.1</p>
<p>Note:Textiles and petrochemicals firm Bombay Dyeing &amp; Manufacturing Co Ltd said other income for the first half included 194 million rupees, representing dividend received from units of Unit Trust of India and interest income related to its manufacturing operations.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
